  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_0' aria-label=\" Gour Acharje versus The State of Tripura & Ors. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('0','2026','2026_6_604_620','2026INSC535'); ><font size='4'> <strong>GOUR ACHARJE<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>THE STATE OF TRIPURA & ORS. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 6 S.C.R. 604</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 535</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010001832026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : PRASHANT KUMAR MISHRA, K.V. VISWANATHAN</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Whether, in a case of death occurring within the absolute privacy of a matrimonial home, the prosecution has established beyond reasonable doubt that the victim&rsquo;s death was a homicidal hanging staged by the appellant-husband after an assault&mdash;thereby shifting facts to the husband&mdash;or whether it was a case of voluntary suicidal hanging as claimed by the appellant. Headnotes&dagger; Penal Code, 1860 &ndash; s.302 &ndash; Victim-deceased, wife of appellant, was subjected to dowry demand by her in-laws &ndash; She was tormented and tortured<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 25-05-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CRIMINAL APPEAL No. 1803/2014</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('0','2026','2026_6_604_620','2026INSC535','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('0','2026','2026_6_604_620','202